  "summary": "Stanford University ended its Flock Safety contract in late July 2026 and is switching to Genetec Cloudrunner, a single-institution ALPR system, citing privacy concerns about Flock's shared network architecture. The article situates the move within a regional wave of Bay Area agencies rethinking Flock, including Santa Cruz, Mountain View, and Santa Clara County, and notes a San Mateo County grand jury finding on data-sharing with private university police.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Stanford University's license plate cameras have been covered up and switched off since late July, when the university quietly ended its contract with Flock Safety and signed with a different vendor.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock is built as a shared network, she said, \"even if that's not how we chose to use it,\" while the new system does not have third-party access built into its architecture.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "A San Mateo County Civil Grand Jury report released Aug. 3 found that at least 12 of the county's 18 police agencies were sharing license plate data with private university security forces, naming Stanford and the University of the Pacific.",
      "paragraph_idx": 24
    }
  ],
